    "body": "I think comparisons to `Py_LIMITED_API` (or `__PYX_LIMITED_VERSION_HEX`) should always be either `Py_LIMITED_API < number` or `Py_LIMITED_API >= number`.  If we do that then it works correctly even if users set `Py_LIMITED_API` to `PY_VERSION_HEX`.\r\n\r\nThe specific comparisons we had that broken that rule weren't quite doing what was intended.",
